# Key Takeaways

* Scaling changes the number of running Pods.
* Deployment defines the desired number of Pods.
* ReplicaSet maintains the desired number of Pods.
* Scale Up creates additional Pods.
* Scale Down removes extra Pods.
* Self-Healing automatically recreates deleted Pods.
* kubelet restarts crashed Containers, not Pods.
* Pod names consist of:

  * Deployment Name
  * ReplicaSet Hash
  * Random Pod ID
* Changing the Pod template creates a new ReplicaSet with a new hash.

